      "id": "q1",
      "kind": "choice",
      "prompt": "A solver returns x with relative residual 1e-16, yet x differs from the true solution in the 3rd digit. The most likely explanation is that",
      "options": [
        "the solver is unstable, since a stable solver would give a 1e-16 error",
        "the matrix is ill-conditioned, so a tiny residual still allows a large error",
        "the right-hand side must be wrong by about 1e-3 in relative terms",
        "the residual was computed in float32, which hides the true residual"
      ],
      "answer": "1",
      "dimension": "C",
      "critical": true,
      "explanation": "Relative error can be as large as kappa times the relative residual; with kappa near 1e13 a 1e-16 residual allows 1e-3 error."
    },
